1. To install the script. open cloud shell and run the following command in the cloud shell:

source <(gsutil cat gs://spls/gsp318/script.sh)



2. Use Cloud Shell to copy the valkyrie-app source code into the ~/valkyrie-app directory. You can use the following command:

gsutil cp gs://spls/gsp318/valkyrie-app.tgz .
tar -xzf valkyrie-app.tgz
cd valkyrie-app



3. The app source code is in valkyrie-app/source.

Create valkyrie-app/Dockerfile and add the configuration below:
FROM golang:1.10
WORKDIR /go/src/app
COPY source .
RUN go install -v
ENTRYPOINT ["app","-single=true","-port=8080"]

4. Use valkyrie-app/Dockerfile to create a Docker image called valkyrie-prod with the tag v0.0.3.

Verify that the Docker image was created by running the following command:

docker images






                                                      OR



# 1. Initialize the lab progress check script
source <(gsutil cat gs://spls/gsp318/script.sh)

